I go to the kirana shop on the corner.
The shop is very small.
An elderly man is sitting there.
I look at my list.
I ask the elderly man.
"Hello, Kaka."
"Hello Madam," Kaka says.
"What do you want?"
"I want turmeric," I say.
Kaka gives me turmeric.
"What else do you want?" he asks.
"I want cumin and salt."
Kaka puts the cumin and salt on the counter.
I like Indian food a lot.
I ask him again.
"Kaka, I also want red chili powder."
"Madam, here is the red chili powder."
"How many rupees is it?" I ask.
"Two hundred and sixty rupees."
I give the money to Kaka.
Now I have all the spices.
